            <div xml:id="d885">

                <pb facs="0812" n="800" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg800"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation (2)/270: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cousins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-07-12T17:00:00-06:00">July 12, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. The Honduran Foreign Office has just informed me that it has received a note
                    warning from the German Minister accredited to this country regarding
                    participation in the Habana Conference. A copy of this note presumably identical
                    with those sent to other Latin American countries which the Secretary of State
                    commented upon yesterday, will be forwarded by air mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cousins</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
